# CC-MC — environment variable reference
#
# This file documents every variable CCMC.Cloud.Api and compose.yaml
# consume. It is a REFERENCE, not something you copy to `.env` directly -
# copy one of the two real mode files instead (PowerShell):
#
#   Copy-Item .env.docker .env -Force   # Mode A: API -> local Docker PostgreSQL
#   Copy-Item .env.neon .env -Force     # Mode B: API -> Neon PostgreSQL
#
# Then (either mode):
#
#   docker compose -p cc-mc up -d --build
#
# `.env`, `.env.docker`, and `.env.neon` are gitignored and must NEVER be
# committed - see .gitignore and README.md "Environment Configuration".
# Only this file (.env.example, placeholders only) is committed.
#
# The application's configuration binding is identical across every
# environment - only these values differ. Names below match exactly what
# CCMC.Cloud.Api/Program.cs reads (ASP.NET Core's double-underscore ->
# nested-config-key convention):

# --- Required by CCMC.Cloud.Api ---------------------------------------------

# Development | Production. Controls Swagger, the DevelopmentSeeder
# (dev-only demo users), and detailed error pages - see appsettings.json's
# own _comment and Program.cs. Development in both .env.docker and .env.neon
# is fine for MVP testing; switch to Production for anything closer to a
# real deployment (this also disables Swagger and the seeder).
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development

# Standard Npgsql keyword connection string. Host is the ONLY thing that
# meaningfully changes between local Docker (the cc-mc-postgres service/
# container hostname) and Neon (Neon's own hostname) - see .env.docker /
# .env.neon.
ConnectionStrings__CcmcDb=Host=REPLACE_ME;Port=5432;Database=REPLACE_ME;Username=REPLACE_ME;Password=REPLACE_ME

# HMAC signing secret for issued JWTs - a long random string, NOT a
# business value, NOT reused between environments. Generate one with e.g.
# `openssl rand -base64 48` (or `[Convert]::ToBase64String((1..48|%{Get-Random -Max 256}))` in PowerShell).
Jwt__Secret=REPLACE_ME

# Kestrel's listen address - explicit here so the container always binds
# 0.0.0.0 (never localhost-only) regardless of the base image's own
# default. Container-internal port stays 8080 in every mode; compose.yaml
# maps a host port to it (see API_HOST_PORT below).
ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://0.0.0.0:8080

# --- Optional (CCMC.Cloud.Api falls back to sensible defaults - see
# JwtOptions.cs / Program.cs - only set these if you need non-default
# values; leaving them unset is fine and is what .env.docker/.env.neon do) ---
# Jwt__Issuer=ccmc-cloud-api
# Jwt__Audience=ccmc-windows-client

# --- Local Docker Compose only (see .env.docker) ----------------------------
# Activates compose.yaml's "docker" profile, which starts the local
# cc-mc-postgres service. Omit entirely in Neon mode.
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=docker
# POSTGRES_USER=
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# POSTGRES_DB=
# POSTGRES_HOST_PORT=

# Host-side port CCMC.Cloud.Api is reachable at from Windows (both modes) -
# the Windows client's CloudApi:BaseUrl points at this port.
# API_HOST_PORT=8081

# --- Windows client (src/CCMC.Desktop/appsettings.json, NOT an env var -
# listed here for completeness of "what changes per environment") ---
# CloudApi:BaseUrl = http://localhost:8081/            (local dev / either Docker Compose mode - API_HOST_PORT above)
# CloudApi:BaseUrl = https://<render-api-domain>/       (future, once Render is deployed - NOT set yet)
